So list comprehensions are one of the more unique features of Python and there are so

00:22.480 --> 00:28.080
popular that other languages have also started implementing list comprehensions as

00:28.080 --> 00:29.080
well.

00:29.080 --> 00:35.440
List comprehensions allow you to take what would normally be quite a lot of code that is

00:35.440 --> 00:39.920
actually pretty common while you're programming, which is going through a list of

00:39.920 --> 00:51.160
items, having a list of results and then appending to your results as you go through a list.

00:51.160 --> 00:57.000
So let's say that we wanted to take a list of names and return a list of the lengths

00:57.000 --> 01:00.080
of those names.

01:00.080 --> 01:04.400
And let's see what this would look like in a Python repel.

01:04.400 --> 01:10.280
Let's do this in a new file.

01:10.280 --> 01:18.040
And I'm going to save this as list comprehensions or list comp stop UI.

